          "# Feature importance from the best individual model (Gradient Boosting)\ngb_model = models['Gradient Boosting']\nif hasattr(gb_model, 'feature_importances_'):\n    importances = gb_model.feature_importances_\nelse:\n    importances = gb_model.named_steps['model'].feature_importances_ if hasattr(gb_model, 'named_steps') else None\n\n# Use Random Forest importances\nrf_model = models['Random Forest']\nimportances = rf_model.feature_importances_\n\nprint(\"\\nPHASE 5: FEATURE IMPORTANCE & INSIGHTS\")\nprint(\"=\"*60)\nprint(\"\\nFeature Importance (Random Forest):\")\nfeat_imp = pd.Series(importances, index=X.columns).sort_values(ascending=False)\nfor feat, imp in feat_imp.items():\n    bar = '\u2588' * int(imp * 50)\n    print(f\"  {feat:<18} {imp:.4f} {bar}\")\n\n# Key insights\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\nprint(\"KEY INSIGHTS FROM THE ANALYSIS\")\nprint(\"=\"*60)\nprint(\"\"\"\n1. GENDER was the strongest predictor: females survived at 75.5%\n   vs males at 24.7% (\"Women and children first\")\n\n2. CLASS mattered: 1st class survival 61.2% vs 3rd class 29.3%\n   (wealth = access to lifeboats)\n\n3. AGE: Children (< 15) had 59.4% survival rate\n\n4. FARE correlates with survival through class and cabin location\n\n5. FAMILY SIZE: Being alone slightly decreased survival chances\n\n6. Best model: Ensemble (AUC=0.896) slightly beat single GB (0.890)\n\"\"\")"
